WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.634 --> 00:00:03.033
-Welcome back to "Late Night."
We're here with Hank Azaria.

00:00:03.033 --> 00:00:04.133
Now, we've been talking about
how you've been doing this

00:00:04.133 --> 00:00:05.434
a long time.
You do not have --

00:00:05.434 --> 00:00:06.934
-A very long time.
-Very long time.

00:00:06.934 --> 00:00:08.367
-I'm very tired.
-You've accomplished --

00:00:08.367 --> 00:00:09.667
[ Light laughter ]

00:00:09.667 --> 00:00:11.667
It's amazing you have
the energy to even be here.

00:00:11.667 --> 00:00:12.968
-It is.
-Based on how long you've been

00:00:12.968 --> 00:00:14.300
doing this.
-Yeah, let's move it along

00:00:14.300 --> 00:00:15.300
because --

00:00:15.300 --> 00:00:16.634
[ Laughter ]

00:00:16.634 --> 00:00:18.834
-You don't have to audition
anymore, but you did --

00:00:18.834 --> 00:00:21.267
and I think this is very helpful
for actors --

00:00:21.267 --> 00:00:24.567
you had an ice breaker
in the audition setting.

00:00:24.567 --> 00:00:26.567
-[ Laughs ] You've done
your research, sir.

00:00:26.567 --> 00:00:28.467
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.
-Yeah.

00:00:28.467 --> 00:00:30.300
Never went well, though,
my "ice breaker."

00:00:30.300 --> 00:00:32.167
-Oh, that's good.
So this is a cautionary tale.

00:00:32.167 --> 00:00:33.634
-Well, I was mentioning earlier,
you know,

00:00:33.634 --> 00:00:34.868
the absurdity of shooting.

00:00:34.868 --> 00:00:36.901
The whole thing
is kind of crazy.

00:00:36.901 --> 00:00:40.133
And, so, often you go into
auditions and they'll say --

00:00:40.133 --> 00:00:41.701
you know, there'll be
the producers and the director

00:00:41.701 --> 00:00:43.133
and people, and say,
"Any questions?

00:00:43.133 --> 00:00:44.334
Do you have any questions?"

00:00:44.334 --> 00:00:47.100
Meaning about the script
or the character.

00:00:47.100 --> 00:00:49.801
And I would say,
"Yeah, um, so,

00:00:49.801 --> 00:00:52.534
I'm supposed to pretend
I'm this guy?"

00:00:52.534 --> 00:00:55.567
[ Laughter ]

00:00:59.067 --> 00:01:05.467
And they would look at me and
they'd go, "Yeah. Yeah."

00:01:05.467 --> 00:01:08.834
And I'd say, "And you're
going to point a camera at it,

00:01:08.834 --> 00:01:11.200
but I'm supposed to pretend
I don't notice that?"

00:01:11.200 --> 00:01:12.734
[ Laughter ]

00:01:12.734 --> 00:01:15.801
And they would go, "Yeah."

00:01:15.801 --> 00:01:19.300
And I would like at them like
they were insane and go, "Okay."

00:01:19.300 --> 00:01:20.734
[ Laughter ]

00:01:20.734 --> 00:01:23.300
Listen, that did much better
than it ever did in the room.

00:01:23.300 --> 00:01:24.701
-Right, right.
Well, that's nice.

00:01:24.701 --> 00:01:26.234
We're completing the circle
here.

00:01:26.234 --> 00:01:28.067
-They would just --
they would look terrified

00:01:28.067 --> 00:01:31.234
and answer earnestly, "Yes,
no, that's right. Yes, yes."

00:01:31.234 --> 00:01:33.434
And then years later,
when I became a producer

00:01:33.434 --> 00:01:35.534
and auditioned a lot of people,
I realized that

00:01:35.534 --> 00:01:37.367
actors are often quite crazy.

00:01:37.367 --> 00:01:39.367
-Yeah.
-So they might actually --

00:01:39.367 --> 00:01:41.267
-They've heard other versions
of that, probably.

00:01:41.267 --> 00:01:43.801
-Oh, you don't know
that somebody is not having

00:01:43.801 --> 00:01:46.234
some kind of psychotic break
in front of you.

00:01:46.234 --> 00:01:48.734
And need to be reminded that,
yes, the camera is going to be

00:01:48.734 --> 00:01:50.801
there, yeah.
-What about -- this is amazing.

00:01:50.801 --> 00:01:53.534
34 -- 34th season
of "The Simpsons."

00:01:53.534 --> 00:01:54.767
[ Cheer and applause ]

00:01:54.767 --> 00:01:57.033
-Yeah, I mean --
-Yeah.

00:01:57.033 --> 00:01:59.167
-Well currently, 34 is airing.

00:01:59.167 --> 00:02:00.767
We're currently making 35.

00:02:00.767 --> 00:02:02.834
But who is counting except
for my business manager.

00:02:02.834 --> 00:02:04.100
-Right, exactly.

00:02:04.100 --> 00:02:07.534
And now how -- how much of
your time is now spent --

00:02:07.534 --> 00:02:09.634
and because, again, you do
so many voices on the show --

00:02:09.634 --> 00:02:11.934
-Yeah.
-Is it -- have you become

00:02:11.934 --> 00:02:15.033
so efficient that you don't have
to work as many hours doing it?

00:02:15.033 --> 00:02:16.300
Or is it exactly
as much time as --

00:02:16.300 --> 00:02:17.834
-[As Moe] I'm going to answer
as Moe, just to --

00:02:17.834 --> 00:02:19.100
-Okay, great, thank you.

00:02:19.100 --> 00:02:21.133
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:21.133 --> 00:02:23.367
-Just 'cause I feel like it.
-Okay.

00:02:23.367 --> 00:02:26.801
-Yeah, I don't -- I barely work,
like, three minutes.

00:02:26.801 --> 00:02:28.834
You know, they show me
the thing, I say the thing,

00:02:28.834 --> 00:02:30.534
and then they send a check,
you know.

00:02:30.534 --> 00:02:32.334
[ Laughter ]

00:02:32.334 --> 00:02:34.067
You know.
-There you go. Nice and easy.

00:02:34.067 --> 00:02:37.300
-[As Comic Book Guy] Sometimes
Comic Book Guy gets involved.

00:02:37.300 --> 00:02:40.801
He says a few things.
Thank you for acknowledging me.

00:02:40.801 --> 00:02:42.501
[ Laughter ]

00:02:42.501 --> 00:02:45.067
-Now, do you get a little
excited when a new one

00:02:45.067 --> 00:02:46.634
comes up, when they come --
I mean --

00:02:46.634 --> 00:02:48.334
-[Normally] It's rare.
-Yeah, at this point,

00:02:48.334 --> 00:02:49.801
I mean, I feel like they don't
want to overwork you.

00:02:49.801 --> 00:02:52.200
There's probably some labor laws
involved of getting --

00:02:52.200 --> 00:02:54.534
-I doubt it.
-Yeah.

00:02:54.534 --> 00:02:57.167
-No, like, I -- you know,
Jim Brockmire is a guy

00:02:57.167 --> 00:02:59.634
that I did on a TV show.

00:02:59.634 --> 00:03:01.300
"Brockmire" is a show I did
for a while.

00:03:01.300 --> 00:03:04.634
And he has now found his way
into the show a little bit.

00:03:04.634 --> 00:03:06.267
-Oh, they -- he's found his way
into the -- that's wonderful.

00:03:06.267 --> 00:03:08.667
-Yeah. I just played a --
some kind of a salesman.

00:03:08.667 --> 00:03:10.667
I don't remember what --
a car salesman.

00:03:10.667 --> 00:03:13.200
And I said, "Ah, let's go with
Jim Brockmire for this one."

00:03:13.200 --> 00:03:14.501
[ Light laughter ]

00:03:14.501 --> 00:03:16.501
So, yeah, but they're --
all the voices are, you know,

00:03:16.501 --> 00:03:18.200
relatives or teachers.
-Yeah.

00:03:18.200 --> 00:03:20.501
-People I grew up with.
-I mean, at what point did

00:03:20.501 --> 00:03:22.601
everybody in
your life realize, "Oh, no"?

00:03:22.601 --> 00:03:24.834
[ Laughter ]

00:03:24.834 --> 00:03:27.868
-Oh, I've had --
there was a guy --

00:03:27.868 --> 00:03:30.334
[As Nat ]I did this character on
"Mad About You"

00:03:30.334 --> 00:03:32.334
called Nat the dog Walker.

00:03:32.334 --> 00:03:33.601
And he talked like this.

00:03:33.601 --> 00:03:35.234
Hey, how you doin' here?

00:03:35.234 --> 00:03:36.734
What's goin' on?

00:03:36.734 --> 00:03:39.734
[Normally] And he was based on
a guy I grew up with,

00:03:39.734 --> 00:03:42.300
who I ran into
while the show was on.

00:03:42.300 --> 00:03:45.934
He said, "Hey!
I saw you on 'Mad About You.'

00:03:45.934 --> 00:03:48.501
How did you think
of that crazy character?"

00:03:48.501 --> 00:03:51.100
[ Laughter ]

00:03:52.367 --> 00:03:54.033
I was like, "I don't know.

00:03:54.033 --> 00:03:57.133
I just kind of draw on
the people I knew in my life."

00:03:57.133 --> 00:04:00.300
And he did not catch on that --
-Well, there you go.

00:04:00.300 --> 00:04:03.367
There you go. Well, it's still
a loving tribute either way.

00:04:03.367 --> 00:04:04.467
-Yeah, let's call it that.

00:04:04.467 --> 00:04:05.467
[ Laughter ]

00:04:05.467 --> 00:04:06.601
-Hey, thanks for being here.

00:04:06.601 --> 00:04:07.701
It's always such a pleasure
to see you.

00:04:07.701 --> 00:04:09.501
-My pleasure.
-Hank Azaria.

00:04:09.501 --> 00:04:11.434
"Hello Tomorrow!" is streaming
on Apple TV+,

00:04:11.434 --> 00:04:12.901
and new episodes
premiering Fridays.

00:04:12.901 --> 00:04:14.467
We'll be right back with
Diane Morgan.

